course: dictionary
lesson: 12283
title: Convene: calling people together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Convene is a formal word, the kind you find in official notices, news reports and serious writing. It means to come together for a meeting, or to call people together for one. «The council convened to discuss the plan.» The councillors came together, so the meeting took place.
explain: Convene is a verb, so its form changes: convenes, convened, convening. Look at the clues to see who is doing what. If people come together for a meeting, they convene. If someone calls them together, that person convenes them. «The headteacher convened a meeting for all parents.» The headteacher called the parents together.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Replace convened with came together for a meeting: "The council came together for a meeting to discuss the plan" still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Convene means to come together for a meeting, or to call people together for one.
fact: «Convened» is the past tense: «The council convened yesterday.»
fact: Convene is formal, so you will meet it more in official notices and serious writing than in everyday chat.
fact: A convenor is a person who calls meetings together.
fact: Convention is a related word to convene, so noticing one can help you spot the other.
exercise: «The club convened in the hall on Monday.» What does convened mean? | *Came together for a meeting | Ate lunch quickly | Painted the walls of the hall | Ran out of the hall
exercise: Mia says convene means to cancel something. What does convene really mean? | To wave goodbye | *To call people together for a meeting | To cancel something | To clean up after a party
exercise: Which word is the past tense of convene? | *convened | convenes | convening | convention
test: «The teachers convene every Friday to plan lessons.» What does convene mean here? | *To come together for a meeting | To cook lunch together | To leave school early
test: Which sentence uses convening correctly? | The sun convened behind the hill. | I convene my bike to school every day. | The dog is convening under the table. | *The committee is convening at noon to vote.
exam: In «The chairman convened the members to vote», what does convened mean? | *Called the members together for a vote | Sent the members home | Forgot about the members | Gave the members a prize
